WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.909 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  today  is victory in europe day  millions rejoice in final and complete  victory after a war lasting nearly six  years  there was delirium euphoria you name it  that it was there amongst those crowds  piccadilly circus was just a vast  cheering sea of faces  it was a really a relief to know that  nobody was shooting us  again  we captured some village and  was announced while we were in this  village that the war had ended  somebody handed me a bottle of brandy i  saw very little  of the rest of the e day  [Music]  it's hard to explain how you can be  overjoyed  at something associated with a war  but the end of a war is a very precious  thing  on d-day itself i was on duty  and passing messages to the troops as  they were landing on the beaches  when they responded to the messages  i could clearly hear the sound of  gunfire  bombs falling men shouting  screams all manner of things  it was total mayhem  the mayhem of war  [Music]  my division that i was in we lost nine  thousand  killed wounded and missing  it's quite frightening to be an  observation tank  and see these tanks going up in flames  i can smell it to this day the smell of  death  and the gunfire continuous gunfire  [Music]  i want the generations to learn a lesson  why do people go and kill them one  another  you only live once  war is such a merciless operation  so that when the end comes yes  you're overjoyed it's over but  afterwards you calculate  the price that was paid for it

